-- title:
--   Jacobian presentation of Ω_{S/R} for a surjection from a polynomial ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $S$ a commutative $R$-algebra, and let $m, r$ be natural numbers. Let $f : \mathrm{Fin}\ r \to R[X_0,\dots,X_{m-1}]$ be a family of polynomials in $m$ variables over $R$, and let $\varphi : R[X_0,\dots,X_{m-1}] \to S$ be an $R$-algebra homomorphism which is assumed surjective and whose kernel is the ideal generated by the range of $f$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an $S$-linear map $\Phi : S^m \to \Omega_{S/R}$ (with $S^m$ the type $\mathrm{Fin}\ m \to S$ of functions, and $\Omega_{S/R}$ Mathlib's module of Kähler differentials) such that: $\Phi$ is surjective; for every index $j$, $\Phi$ sends the $j$-th standard basis vector $\mathrm{Pi.single}\ j\ 1$ to $d(\varphi(X_j))$; and the kernel of $\Phi$ is the $S$-submodule spanned by the $r$ vectors indexed by $i$, the $i$-th being $j \mapsto \varphi(\partial f_i/\partial X_j)$, i.e. the rows of the Jacobian matrix of $f$ read through $\varphi$. Only the existence of such a $\Phi$ is asserted, not a canonical choice.
--
--   This is the second fundamental (conormal) exact sequence in the concrete form of a Jacobian presentation of the module of Kähler differentials of a finitely presented algebra, stated for an arbitrary surjection $\varphi$ from a polynomial ring rather than for the quotient map. It is used in the computation of the Jacobian determinant attached to a $p$-divisible group over a ring of integers, in [`PDivisibleGroup.associated_jacobianDet_pow_of_hasDimension_of_ringOfIntegers`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.associated_jacobianDet_pow_of_hasDimension_of_ringOfIntegers).
